+- ✅ **Phase 7 — shipped** (`src/App.jsx` Home + `SUPPORT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER` export, `src/RapidCupPrizeCollection.jsx` RapidCupHelpButton, `src/LeagueDetail.jsx` myUsername plumbing)
+  - **History archive:** no new code needed — `isLeagueCompleted()` already treats `format === "knockout"` (what `generate_rapid_cup_bracket` creates every Rapid Cup league as) as completed once the bracket is down to one winner, so a finished Rapid Cup automatically moves into `CompletedLeaguesPage` the same way every other league does, with the same read-only reopen via `onOpen`. Verified against a live Supabase test league.
+  - **Help button → WhatsApp:** new `RapidCupHelpButton` inside `RapidCupTournamentExtras` (renders for any Rapid Cup league, not gated behind having played a fixture yet), reusing the existing `waLink`/`WHATSAPP_GREEN` helpers and the site's one `SUPPORT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER` (now exported from App.jsx for this). Prefilled message includes "Rapid Cup", the player's username (threaded down as a new `myUsername` prop on `RapidCupTournamentExtras`), and a direct `?league=<id>` link back into the tournament.
+  - **Home banner mount:** `RapidCupBanner` is now imported and rendered in `Home`, directly under the Quick Actions tile row and above the League Ladder section, per Section 12. `onOpenLeague` reuses the same `onOpen` handler every other league card on Home already uses; there's no dedicated lobby page yet, so `onOpenLobby` (tapping the banner body before it's full/live) is just a toast nudge toward the Join button rather than real navigation.
+  - Verified with a clean `npm run build` (1583 modules, no errors) — the `LeagueDetail`/`RapidCupPrizeCollection` lazy chunk importing `waLink`/`SUPPORT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER` from `App.jsx` bundles fine, same pattern `LeagueLadderDetail.jsx` already uses.
+  - **Not done (deliberately out of scope for this pass):** no dedicated "Rapid Cup" badge/label on `LeagueCard` or a bespoke completed-Rapid-Cup summary (pool size, per-player fees) in `CompletedLeaguesPage` — the plan's own Section 9 wording ("same pattern as CompletedLeaguesPage") reads as "reuse the existing generic display", and the generic knockout-format card already shows team count, played/fixtures, and the leader without erroring on Rapid Cup's null `members.entry_fee`. Worth a follow-up if you want Rapid Cup to look visually distinct in the archive rather than just another knockout league.
